#7, account management. "Forgot password?" is a dead href="#". "Change password" shows a "Soon" badge. The profile page is still the disabled "Phase 2" button, and teachers have no profile page. session_service.end_all_sessions() exists, ready for a password change, but nothing calls it.
#9, grade rules. GRADE_POINTS is unchanged, with no C-, D+, W or I. Nothing stops the same course being added twice, since there's no unique constraint on the record, semester and course.
#10, lists and search. list_for_teacher still builds f"%{search}%" without escaping % or _. There's no pagination, no filters and no export.
#11, audit trail. Deletes are still hard db.delete() calls, and there's no audit or history table.
#12, sign-in flow. require_guest only checks for a student session, so a signed-in teacher visiting /login still sees the student form. There is one auth_token per browser, so signing in as one role still revokes the other.
#13, headers and deploy. No CSP, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy or HSTS anywhere, and no Dockerfile. The --proxy-headers advice is in the README and in a client_ip comment, but nothing in the code enforces it.
#15, tooling and docs. No ruff config, no CI and no pyproject.toml. The README's Tests section still says 18 tests, but the suite now has about 180 test functions. Its project-structure tree also only lists the student module. The README does now cover the teacher, admin and grades features in prose.